#. Type: string
#. Description
#: ../kerbridge-config.templates:2001
msgid "Kerberos realm for this deployment:"
msgstr ""

#. Type: string
#. Description
#: ../kerbridge-config.templates:2001
msgid ""
" KerBridge serves one Kerberos realm.\n"
" Give it in upper case, for example EXAMPLE.SITE.\n"
" KerBridge derives other values from it: the domain root,\n"
" the DNS domain, the NetBIOS name, the short name of the\n"
" domain controller, and two organizational units."
msgstr ""

#. Type: string
#. Description
#: ../kerbridge-config.templates:2001
msgid ""
" You cannot correct the realm later.\n"
" It goes into the Samba database,\n"
" and the permissions of every file carry an identifier from it.\n"
" This is binary data in many places, and no edit can change it.\n"
" To use a different realm, provision the domain again."
msgstr ""

#. Type: string
#. Description
#: ../kerbridge-config.templates:2001
msgid ""
" KerBridge writes the initial config files\n"
" on the first installation only.\n"
" If you leave this empty, it writes nothing."
msgstr ""

#. Type: error
#. Description
#: ../kerbridge-config.templates:3001
msgid "Invalid Kerberos realm"
msgstr ""

#. Type: error
#. Description
#: ../kerbridge-config.templates:3001
msgid ""
" A realm is a domain name with dots and no spaces,\n"
" for example EXAMPLE.SITE.\n"
" Your value is not a realm name."
msgstr ""

#. Type: string
#. Description
#: ../kerbridge-config.templates:4001
msgid "LDAPS URL of the domain controller:"
msgstr ""

#. Type: string
#. Description
#: ../kerbridge-config.templates:4001
msgid ""
" KerBridge binds to this address.\n"
" It accepts ldaps:// only, because plain LDAP and StartTLS\n"
" send the bind password and each password write in clear text."
msgstr ""

#. Type: string
#. Description
#: ../kerbridge-config.templates:4001
msgid ""
" The proposed address uses a domain controller with the name\n"
" \"kerbridge\" in the realm above.\n"
" Change the host name if yours is different."
msgstr ""

#. Type: error
#. Description
#: ../kerbridge-config.templates:5001
msgid "Invalid LDAPS URL"
msgstr ""

#. Type: error
#. Description
#: ../kerbridge-config.templates:5001
msgid ""
" The address must start with ldaps://.\n"
" KerBridge refuses plain ldap:// and StartTLS.\n"
" An address in that form fails later."
msgstr ""

#. Type: select
#. Description
#: ../kerbridge-config.templates:6001
msgid "Cloud identity provider for this deployment:"
msgstr ""

#. Type: select
#. Description
#: ../kerbridge-config.templates:6001
msgid ""
" KerBridge admits the users of one cloud IdP per source.\n"
" This writes the source file for the one you choose."
msgstr ""

#. Type: select
#. Description
#: ../kerbridge-config.templates:6001
msgid ""
" Choose none for a host that does no synchronization\n"
" and serves no sign-ins, for example an administrator machine\n"
" with kerbridge-manage.\n"
" KerBridge then writes the config files\n"
" with no identity provider in them."
msgstr ""

#. Type: select
#. Description
#: ../kerbridge-config.templates:6001
msgid ""
" Nothing else about the provider is asked here.\n"
" The identifiers that name your tenant and its applications\n"
" are lines to complete in /etc/kerbridge/idp_<name>.toml,\n"
" and `kbconfig check` lists every one of them at once."
msgstr ""
